<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Helier</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as St Helier</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Helier is the capital and largest town of Jersey, on St Aubin's Bay on the island's south coast. It is named after Helier, a sixth-century hermit venerated as the island's patron saint. The seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/states-of-jersey">States of Jersey</a> and the Royal Court, it was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jersey">Battle of Jersey</a> in 1781 and grew in the nineteenth century with trade, tourism and English settlers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-helier.jpg" alt="Saint Helier" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Man vyi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_H%C3%A9lyi_p%C3%A8lerinnage_2011_08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
